<http://data.silknow.org/object/edc2f56b-f54d-3a32-9c9d-f9024dba069d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Picture woven in silk and mounted on card. With two victorious generals, Wellington and Blücher, meeting after the Battle of Waterloo. The design is taken from a painting by Daniel Maclise. The generals are shaking hands amidst a scene of carnage outside the inn called 'Le Belle Alliance'. Woven mainly in blue, red and brown silk. On a grey mount inscribed 'Wellington &amp; Blücher' and 'Meeting after the battle of Waterloo'. No trade label on the back of the mount."@en , "Picture 'Wellington & Blücher' woven in silk and mounted on card, designed by E. Krefeld Birmes, Germany, ca. 1850"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/8971586d-f4c0-36ca-94c5-cbe8e67c304e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Picture 'Wellington & Blücher' woven in silk and mounted on card, designed by E. Krefeld Birmes, Germany, ca. 1850"@en , "Picture woven in silk and mounted on card. With two victorious generals, Wellington and Blücher, meeting after the Battle of Waterloo. The design is taken from a painting by Daniel Maclise. The generals are shaking hands amidst a scene of carnage outside the inn called 'Le Belle Alliance'. Woven mainly in blue, red and brown silk. On a grey mount inscribed 'Wellington &amp; Blücher' and 'Meeting after the battle of Waterloo'. No trade label on the back of the mount."@en ;
